{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1427617-slavic-mythology-changeling-and-house-varich","id":1427617,"title":"Slavic mythology, changeling and house Varich","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-07T11:29:48-08:00","id":1427617,"title":"Slavic mythology, changeling and house Varich","content":"So im playing in a online venue game, and im gravitating towards playing a sidhe from house varich.<br /> <br /> So I guess I have a couple of questions for the more experienced players.<br /> <br /> Is there any canon information on slavic changelings, and how they interact with the world of darkness as a whole?<br /> What about slavic mythology? Do the varich have their own stories or names for the Tuatha de Danaan, Fomorians and that sort of thing?<br /> And what do the Varich view themselves as in relation to their native mythology?<br /> <br /> Im a bit of a noob, so if this stuff is already answered or irrelevant feel free to point that out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25428-ebtard","name":"Ebtard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T12:30:42-08:00","id":1427619,"title":"","content":"For this, I'd suggest getting your hands on Book of Lost Houses, which currently has the most information on House Varich, how they see the world, and some unique Slavic Inanimae. There's also a little in the C20 corebook on their native lands. (The big thing with pre-V5 Russia is that it was mainly subject to Vampire and Werewolf metaplot, dominated by the Nosferatu Baba Yaga.)<br /> <br /> But in brief, the Varich see their (still-active) founder as the son of Sun and Moon, or as they call them Dazboga and Miesiac. The Tuatha de Danaan they know as the Vila, who count Dazboga and Miesiac among their number. The story of the House's founding holds that it was a mark of recognition from the Vila following Varich's near-fatal battle with the Fomorian Marena, which ended with him imprisoning her.<br /> <br /> No info on how they see themselves in relation to their native mythology, though they've been worshiped as gods by their Dreamers. In their own telling, they originated with the dreams of Russia's first peoples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T19:58:04-08:00","id":1427670,"title":"","content":"Most of what you'd think of as traditional Slavic fay have been relegated to Inanimae according to official stuff for Varich, but the majority work well as Kith either as variants of standard Kith or made up wholecloth. eg. Vila are pretty much Sidhe that have heavily invested in Metamorphosis, Domovoi/Kikimora work well as Boggans ( Domovoi are used as an example Kith in C20)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T12:32:32-08:00","id":1427738,"title":"","content":"@marin<br /> <br /> Would ou mind elaborating on what the Book of Lost Houses says is unique about Slavic Inanimae ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T23:37:34-08:00","id":1427815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1427617-slavic-mythology-changeling-and-house-varich?p=1427738#post1427738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@marin<br /> <br /> Would ou mind elaborating on what the Book of Lost Houses says is unique about Slavic Inanimae ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more that the Varich chapter has some unique Inanimae which only appear in that chapter.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T23:42:03-08:00","id":1427816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1427617-slavic-mythology-changeling-and-house-varich?p=1427815#post1427815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's more that the Varich chapter has some unique Inanimae which only appear in that chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Most of the relevant info is here: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/House_Varich#Inanimae:_Spirits_of_the_Rus\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ho...its_of_the_Rus</a><br /> <br /> Honestly I think quite a few of them work better as Kith, and theres a Domovoi Kith in C20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T06:13:30-08:00","id":1427850,"title":"","content":"Along with the Inanimae, the Adhene/Denizens all fit well as Slavic fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}